hub.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T16:19:31Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T16:27:50Z","body":"Tested the previous RegEx again. It seems to be hardcoded to detect paths starting with `/` or `\\`, or else it doesn't match anything. `/usr/bin/code` works but just `code` or `code.exe` doesn't.\r\n\r\nExec Path is supposed to work with PATH commands, therefore autoset should consider commands without a backslash too.\r\n\r\n> The only one that didn't work for me was Rider, other paths work fine on Windows at least. I assume the issue is mostly on other platforms.\r\n\r\nI think we have an answer now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3433209076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3437870506","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111820#issuecomment-3437870506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111820","id":3437870506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M6b2q","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followe